  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -10 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $B$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $B$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -10 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,5\\,\\, & 5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,5\\,\\, & 5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=5$ and ${u}_{23}=-3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=5\\cdot (-3)=-15.\n$$",
